te contratos en áreas distintas. Se puede analizar si los contratos adjudicados en diciembre están relacionados con un mismo tipo de servicio o suministro.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 47 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 14.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.3 to 4.9. December accounts for 13% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 6. Contract [1], for 14,986.12 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. Statistical patterns can reflect normal market behavior or budget constraints, not wrongdoing. The data alone does not show intent or violation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts to see if they align with usual patterns. Review awardee A’s contracts to identify if multiple contracts serve the same need. Look at the December contracts to determine if they were part of a larger procurement strategy.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["QkSbUt0BUYnECtSnloz%2BZQ%3D%3D","zSvu44iwkQacTfjQf3USOg%3D%3D","0pD%2ByHjfjjOExvMJXBMHHQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}